---
import CaseLayout from '../../layouts/CaseLayout.astro';
import SignalChain from '../../components/SignalChain.astro';
import { clearExgLimits } from '../../lib/projects';
---

<CaseLayout slug="clear-exg">
  <section>
    <h2>The problem</h2>
    <p class="muted">
      Seizure diagnosis still depends on a clinical EEG: a technician, a cap of
      wet electrodes and a room. Roughly 2.9 million U.S. adults live with active
      epilepsy, at about $24 billion in annual healthcare spending, and most of
      that monitoring happens in short windows that may never overlap with an
      event.
    </p>
    <p class="muted">
      Moving the electronics into an earbud means the front-end has to survive on
      a battery you would actually wear. An EEG signal is tens of microvolts;
      mains hum is millivolts; the electrode-tissue interface drifts. The chain
      has to reject all of that and still fit in a power budget measured in
      hundreds of microwatts.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>The chain</h2>
    <SignalChain />
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Why subthreshold</h2>
    <p class="muted">
      An OTA-C filter puts its corner at <code>f₀ = gm / 2πC</code>. To land at
      100 Hz with an on-chip capacitor of a few picofarads, the transconductance
      has to be tiny — nanosiemens. In strong inversion that is impossible without
      an absurd capacitor. In subthreshold, <code>gm = I<sub>D</sub> / nV<sub>T</sub></code>,
      so a 10 nA bias buys exactly the gm needed, and the power falls out of it:
      the EEG low-pass runs on <strong>37.44 nW</strong>.
    </p>
    <p class="muted">
      That is the whole reason the beta-multiplier reference matters. It is the
      block that generates those nanoampere currents stably across process and
      temperature, and every filter corner on the chip inherits its accuracy.
      There is a live model of this on the
      <a href="/#playground">playground</a> — drag the bias current and watch the
      corner move.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>What it measured</h2>
    <div class="tbl">
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th>Parameter</th><th>Result</th><th>Block</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Total gain</td><td>80 dB</td><td>Full chain</td></tr>
          <tr><td>CMRR</td><td>100 dB</td><td>Chopper CCIA</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Total power</td><td>427 µW</td><td>Full chain</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Quiescent current</td><td>115.4 µA</td><td>Full chain</td></tr>
          <tr><td>EEG low-pass corner</td><td>101.3 Hz @ 10.4 nA</td><td>OTA-C biquad</td></tr>
          <tr><td>ECG low-pass corner</td><td>249.6 Hz @ 26 nA</td><td>OTA-C biquad</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Notch depth</td><td>−18.67 dB @ 63.1 Hz</td><td>4th-order notch</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Notch power</td><td>91.2 nW @ 2.67 nA</td><td>4th-order notch</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Bias current range</td><td>2.6 – 40 nA</td><td>Beta-multiplier ref</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Gain stage</td><td>87 dB, PM 87.76°, UGB 8.75 MHz</td><td>Folded cascode</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>What it did not do</h2>
    <p class="muted">
      Three targets were missed, and they are the first things I would attack in
      a second pass:
    </p>
    <ul class="limits">
      {clearExgLimits.map((l) => <li>{l}</li>)}
    </ul>
    <p class="muted">
      The noise number is the important one. Chopping moves flicker noise out of
      band but the input devices still have to be sized for it, and I traded
      area away too early. That is a sizing decision, not a topology problem.
    </p>
  </section>
</CaseLayout>

<style>
  h2 { font-size: clamp(1.4rem, 2.6vw, 1.9rem); margin-bottom: 1rem; }
  code { font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 0.9em; color: var(--accent); }
  a { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--accent); }

  .tbl { overflow-x: auto; border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 4px; }
  table { border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; min-width: 34rem; font-size: 0.9rem; }
  th, td { text-align: left; padding: 0.7rem 1rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }
  thead th {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 0.64rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--fg-3);
    background: var(--bg-2);
  }
  tbody tr:last-child td { border-bottom: 0; }
  td:nth-child(2) { font-family: var(--mono); color: var(--accent); white-space: nowrap; }
  td:nth-child(3) { color: var(--fg-3); }

  .limits { margin: 1.25rem 0 1.5rem; padding-left: 1.1rem; color: var(--fg-2); display: grid; gap: 0.5rem; }
  .limits li::marker { color: var(--accent); }
</style>
